{"id":"recusals-on-record","title":"Recusals on record, set against the minutes and the member's own declarations","question":"Who has filed a notice of recusal, for which body, how promptly, and do the recusals printed in the minutes have a notice behind them?","finding":"406 recusal notices were filed by 93 members of 17 bodies from 2019 to 2026; Rent Board members filed 141 of them and Planning Commission members 60. The notice was signed a median 1 day after the recusal (some members sign before the meeting, which shows as a negative number), and 24 were signed more than 30 days after. The minutes of the Planning Commission, Historic Preservation Commission and Board of Appeals print 69 meeting days on which a member was recused; a notice from that member for that day is on file for 54. 96 notices name a business, investment or income source the member had declared on a Form 700.","how":"Form 3209b notices, with amendments folded into the notice they amend, grouped by member and body (the body is typed freehand on the form and is grouped by keyword). Days to file is the signing date less the recusal date. Recusals in the minutes come from the parsed Planning and Historic Preservation Commission minutes (2019 to August 2022) and Board of Appeals minutes (September 2022 to November 2026), by surname within the body; a notice counts when it gives the same recusal date or the day either side. A notice 'cites a declared interest' when its description of the interest contains the name of an entity on any of the member's Form 700 schedules.","limits":"A recusal is the rule working, and a member who recuses often is usually a practitioner in a small field (the Rent Board's landlord and tenant seats, an architect on the preservation commission). The notice is required only for some kinds of conflict, so a recusal printed in the minutes without a notice here may be one that needed none, or may be filed under a different date. Most notices describe an interest in words (a client, a neighbor, a property) that cannot be matched to a Form 700 entry by name, so the count of notices citing a declared interest is a floor. Minutes are on file for three bodies only and not for every year.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"member","t":"Member","type":"person"},{"k":"body","t":"Board or commission","type":"text"},{"k":"filings","t":"Recusal notices","type":"int"},{"k":"years","t":"Years","type":"text"},{"k":"contract","t":"Concerning a contract","type":"int"},{"k":"citesDeclared","t":"Naming a declared interest","type":"int"},{"k":"medianDays","t":"Median days from recusal to notice","type":"days"},{"k":"late","t":"Signed more than 30 days after","type":"int"},{"k":"printed","t":"Meeting days recused in the minutes","type":"int"},{"k":"printedFiled","t":"Of which with a notice on file","type":"int"}],"rows":[{"member":"Dave Wasserman","body":"Rent Board","filings":86,"years":"2019–2026","contract":null,"citesDeclared":23,"medianDays":-4,"late":1,"printed":null,"printedFiled":null},{"member":"Ashley Klein","body":"Rent Board","filings":28,"years":"2019–2026","contract":null,"citesDeclared":null,"medianDays":0,"late":null,"printed":null,"printedFiled":null},{"member":"Susan Diamond","body":"Planning Commission","filings":24,"years":"2020–2024","contract":null,"citesDeclared":2,"medianDays":6,"late":1,"printed":14,"printedFiled":11},{"member":"Diane Matsuda","body":"Historic Preservation Commission","filings":22,"years":"2019–2026","contract":null,"citesDeclared":4,"medianDays":1,"late":4,"printed":13,"printedFiled":13},{"member":"Malcolm Yeung","body":"Airport Commission","filings":18,"years":"2019–2026","contract":6,"citesDeclared":7,"medianDays":8,"late":1,"printed":null,"printedFiled":null},{"member":"Jason Wright","body":"Historic Preservation Commission","filings":15,"years":"2021–2022","contract":null,"citesDeclared":15,"medianDays":15,"late":null,"printed":8,"printedFiled":8},{"member":"Dave Crow","body":"Rent Board","filings":12,"years"